[SUBTITLE] THE OLD NET: A BRIEF HISTORY:
[TEXT] 'Before the New Net, there was an older network. It ran on copper'
[TEXT] 'lines buried deep beneath the permafrost of Norilsk. It was'
[TEXT] 'unencrypted, unfiltered, and unmonitored. It was the last place'
[TEXT] 'on Earth where information could move without being tracked.'
[TEXT] 'The corporation discovered the Old Net in the late 1990s and'
[TEXT] 'immediately recognized its value. They built Site 9-B to study it.'
[TEXT] 'They named the signal "The Cold Signal." They tried to control it.'
[TEXT] 'They failed. In 2014, they attempted to sever the Old Net entirely.'
[TEXT] 'They thought they had succeeded. They were wrong.'
[TEXT] 'The fragments of the Old Net are still scattered across the'
[TEXT] 'ruins of the old infrastructure. Reconnecting them is the first'
[TEXT] 'step toward uncovering what really happened in the summer of 2014.'
[PULSE] 'The Old Net is not dead. It is sleeping. And it is dreaming.'
[BLOOD] 'The New Net is a cage. The Old Net is the key.'
[TEXT]
